# This repository ships a flasher and prebuilt images. Everything needed to
# convert a camera is: README.md, asecam-flash.py, images/.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT: per-device flash dumps.
# mtd3/mtd4/mtd5 hold per-unit serials, calibration and network config, and the
# full-flash images contain all of it. They are also the ONLY way back to stock
# for a given camera -- so keep them safe locally, just not in a repository.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
backups/
readback/
.stage/
*_fullflash_*.bin
*_mtd[0-9]_*.bin

# Build trees (multi-gigabyte, regenerable) -- build from the source repos,
# see README.md "Building it yourself".
src/
output/
output-*/
initramfs/root/
initramfs/init
initramfs/images.h
initramfs/.config.production

# Development scratch from the original conversion work. The shipped tool is
# asecam-flash.py; these are kept locally but are not part of the release.
flash_net.py
flash_fh8856.py
identify.py
find_cams.py
tftpd.py
make_env.py
rescue_131.py
env_set_at_prompt.py
ctel.py
cssh.py
uart.sh
tftproot/
tools/
report/
re/
patches/
HANDOFF.md
REPORT.md
FULLHAN-SDK-NOTES.md
openipcissuedraft.md

# Logs, caches, editors
*.log
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
flash-pins.jpg
restore_vendor.py
